Yes, that is very good.  Most of my fighting involves leaning on the
keyboard, but I'm always prepared to use non-melee options if
necessary.  For example, I generally use ranged against monsters with
dangerous special attacks (i.e. footrice), or monsters that do way too
much damage (i.e. mumak).  However, most of the monsters in the game
really aren't a threat to melee characters, and using ranged against
them is a waste of time.

Personally, I think using ranged attacks as your main strategy is a
death trap.  You won't learn the general damage the monsters do, or
what their special attacks do.  Therefore, when you finally get thrown
in the middle of a bunch of monsters, you don't really know how to deal
with it well.  The best example is monsters that can summon other
monsters.  Someone that only uses ranged attacks probably won't be able
to deal with this very well.  They won't know if the monsters around
them are dangerous, they won't know which monsters they should plow
through to get closer to the summoner, and the easy way out (spam
Elebereth) which just cause a lot of chaos, and won't help them get
near the summoner.



